    ],
    "steps": [
     "Cut the tofu into 2 cm cubes and leave them in hot water while you start the sauce.",
     "Heat the oil in the wok over medium heat. Fry the pork until crumbly and starting to brown.",
     "Add the doubanjiang and fry until the oil turns red. Add the black beans, garlic, ginger and chili flakes for a few seconds.",
     "Pour in the stock with the soy sauce and sugar. Slide in the drained tofu and simmer gently for 4 to 5 minutes, pushing rather than stirring.",
     "Mix the cornstarch with a little cold water and stir it in until the sauce clings to the tofu.",
     "Scatter with the scallion and the ground Sichuan pepper."
    ]
   },
   "cardId": "card-mapo-tofu",
   "notes": "Dunlop 2019 (ma po dou fu); Chengdu 2010. Numbing comes from the peppercorn, not the paste; the paste brings heat and the deep red colour."
